References: <416EBDA5D6A5944B9C247760960828690E8BA98C@UTDEX23.campus.ad.utdallas.edu>
Message-ID: <A94E707B-D0BA-4ADE-9E20-10D9632073AF@iq.harvard.edu>

In order to compute first differences and risk ratios, you need two "setx" objects. For example:

  x.out <- setx(MH6)
  x1.out <- setx(MH6, L_PC_PRODUCTION = 1)
  sim(MH6, x = x.out, x1 = x1.out)

I'm not sure of the status of the plotting functions for relogit. The plot you are looking for simply may not be implemented.

However, still try:
    plot(MH6)


